examples.question_text:
The Venn diagram records the instruments played by 30 students. $P$ means piano and $G$ means guitar.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (7,4);
\draw (2.5,2) circle (1.5);
\draw (4.5,2) circle (1.5);
\path (1.5,3.6) node {$P$} (5.5,3.6) node {$G$};
\path (1.8,2) node {$10$} (3.5,2) node {$6$} (5.2,2) node {$9$} (6.4,0.5) node {$5$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the probability that a randomly selected student plays:
a. both instruments
b. piano only
c. piano or guitar, or both
d. piano or guitar, but not both
e. no piano
f. neither instrument
g. at least one instrument
h. more than one instrument
i. at most one instrument.

examples.solution_text:
Place the 8 students who play both in the overlap. Subtract them from each sport total.
$\begin{align*}\text{Cricket only}&=24-8=16\\\text{Soccer only}&=18-8=10\\\text{Neither}&=40-(16+8+10)=6\end{align*}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (7,4);
\draw (2.5,2) circle (1.5);
\draw (4.5,2) circle (1.5);
\path (1.5,3.6) node {$C$} (5.5,3.6) node {$S$};
\path (1.8,2) node {$16$} (3.5,2) node {$8$} (5.2,2) node {$10$} (6.4,0.5) node {$6$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$C$ represents cricket and $S$ represents soccer. The outside region contains 6 students.
$P(\text{neither})=\frac6{40}=\frac3{20}$.

First find how many play at least one instrument. The two instrument totals count students who play both twice.
$\begin{align*}\text{At least one}&=48-6=42\\\text{Both}&=29+25-42=12\\\text{Piano only}&=29-12=17\\\text{Guitar only}&=25-12=13\end{align*}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},draw=black]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (7,4);
\draw (2.5,2) circle (1.5);
\draw (4.5,2) circle (1.5);
\path (1.5,3.6) node {$P$} (5.5,3.6) node {$G$};
\path (1.8,2) node {$17$} (3.5,2) node {$12$} (5.2,2) node {$13$} (6.4,0.5) node {$6$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
a. Exclusive or excludes both and neither: $P(\text{exactly one})=\frac{17+13}{48}=\frac58$.
b. At most one also includes neither: $P(\text{at most one})=\frac{17+13+6}{48}=\frac34$.

